    "scope": "12.i.W first passive JUnit preparation: exact original files, raw/canonical provenance, caller-declared tool/version and actual importer version; explicit abort or diagnosed subset with complete occurrence accounting. Neither policy converts failed measurements into passed Evidence. Malformed global inputs remain fatal, and no file/network/process/clock or host configuration is used. Persistence and complete import authority remain open. 12.i.R additionally binds exact Generic/SARIF originals and applies explicit abort/skip to record-local required-field, binding and mapping failures. Every source occurrence is accepted, rejected with diagnostics or withheld by abort; conflicting or ambiguous observations cannot select a favorable result. Global envelope/source/target/resource errors remain fatal; no persistence or external authority is granted."
